Enforcement Decree of the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Registration of Establishment)
The matters to be registered upon the establishment of the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Corporation") are as follows:
1. Purpose;
2. Name;
3. Location of its principal office;
4. Capital;
5. Names and addresses of its executive officers;
6. Method of public notice.

Article 3 (Registration of Establishment of Branches, etc.)
Where the Corporation establishes a branch, sub-branch, or office (hereinafter referred to as "branches, etc."), it shall register the name, location, and date of establishment of the branch, etc. at the location of its principal office within two weeks after its establishment.

Article 4 (Registration of Relocation)
(1) Where the Corporation relocates its principal office, it shall register the new location and the date of relocation at the former or new location within two weeks after the relocation.
(2) Where the Corporation relocates a branch, etc., it shall register the new location and the date of relocation at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the relocation.

Article 5 (Registration of Changes)
Where any matter registered under any subparagraph of Article 2 or under Article 3 changes (excluding a change subject to registration of relocation under Article 4), the Corporation shall register the changed matter at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the change.

Article 6 (Registration of Appointment of Agents, etc.)
(1) Where its president appoints an agent under Article 7 of the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), the Corporation shall register the following matters at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the appointment. The same shall apply where any registered matter changes. <Amended on January 21, 2025>
1. Name and address of the agent;
2. Name and location of the principal office or branch, etc. to which the agent is assigned;
3. Details of any restrictions imposed on the agent's authority.
(2) Where its president dismisses an agent appointed under Article 7 of the Act, the Corporation shall register the dismissal at the location of its principal office within two weeks after the dismissal. <Amended on January 21, 2025>

Article 7 (Documents to Be Attached to Applications for Registration)
An application for registration under Articles 2 through 6 shall be accompanied by the documents specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Registration of establishment under Article 2: The articles of incorporation of the Corporation and documents certifying the amount of capital contributions and the qualifications of its executive officers;
2. Registration of establishment of branches, etc. under Article 3: Documents certifying the establishment of the branch, etc.;
3. Registration of relocation under Article 4: Documents certifying the relocation of the principal office or branch, etc.;
4. Registration of changes under Article 5: Documents certifying the changed matters;
5. Registration of the appointment, change, or dismissal of an agent under Article 6: The following documents:
(a) Documents certifying the appointment, change, or dismissal of the agent;
(b) Where the agent's authority is restricted under Article 6 (1) 3, documents certifying the restrictions.

Article 8 (Commencement of Registration Period)
Where any matter to be registered under this Decree requires authorization or approval from the Minister of Trade and Industry, the registration period shall commence on the date the applicant receives the documents concerning that authorization or approval. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 9 (Loans)
(1) The funds lent under Article 8 (1) 11 of the Act are as follows:
1. Mining funds;
2. Funds for the stone and aggregate industries;
3. Funds for processing and stockpiling mineral products.
(2) Loans of the mining funds referred to in paragraph (1) 1 shall be secured by the mining rights and mining facilities of the mine for which the loan is granted: Provided, That other property may be accepted as collateral in lieu of those mining rights and mining facilities in any of the following cases:
1. Where recovery from damage caused by a natural disaster or any other comparable cause, or the development of a mine, is urgent;
2. Where drainage or restoration of mine galleries is to be undertaken to redevelop a mine;
3. Where a third party's security right has been established over the mining rights and mining facilities of the mine for which the loan is granted;
4. Where a loan equal to or greater than the value appraised under paragraph (3) is to be granted;
5. Where a loan is to be granted to a mining leaseholder;
6. Where a loan is to be granted for the development of overseas mineral resources or deep seabed mineral resources;
7. Any of the following cases in which it is deemed difficult to recover the funds lent with only the mining rights and mining facilities as collateral:
(a) Where mining facilities necessary for the development of the mine cannot be provided as collateral;
(b) Where the credit standing of the mining right holder, including its financial and management conditions, falls below the standards determined by the president of the Corporation.
(3) When accepting mining rights as collateral under the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of paragraph (2), the Corporation shall determine reserves, grades, and other relevant matters through surveys of geology and mineral deposits (meaning portions of the ground containing large concentrations of useful minerals) and appraise the mine.
(4) In cases falling under the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of paragraph (2), the Corporation shall also examine the feasibility of the loan by applying, mutatis mutandis, the method specified in paragraph (3).
(5) The interest rate on funds lent by the Corporation shall be the rate determined by the Minister of Trade and Industry in consultation with the Minister of Planning and Budget. <Amended on October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025>

Article 10 (Management of Loans of Mining Funds, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 10 (2) of the Act, the Corporation shall undertake the management necessary to ensure that the funds lent under Article 8 (1) 11 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "loans of mining funds, etc.") are used for the purposes of the loans.
(2) In any of the following cases, the Corporation may, pursuant to paragraph (1), require a recipient of loans of mining funds, etc. to take appropriate measures for the management of such loans, including the provision of additional collateral:
1. Where loans of mining funds, etc. have been used for purposes other than the purposes of the loans;
2. Where it is deemed difficult to recover loans of mining funds, etc. due to deterioration of the financial structure resulting from poor management of the relevant business, or loss, damage, disposal, or other impairment of the collateral.
(3) The Corporation may demand that a person who fails to take measures under the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of paragraph (2) repay all or part of the loans of mining funds, etc., even before the repayment due date.

Article 11 (Bearing of Project Expenses)
(1) Project expenses that the Corporation may require relevant institutions or beneficiaries to bear pursuant to Article 9 (1) of the Act shall consist of the following costs incurred for the relevant project:
1. Material costs;
2. Personnel costs;
3. Expenses such as electricity and water charges;
4. General administrative expenses;
5. An amount determined by the president of the Corporation in consultation with the relevant institutions or beneficiaries for costs comparable to those specified in subparagraphs 1 through 4.
(2) The president of the Corporation shall determine and publicly announce the standards for calculating project expenses under paragraph (1) for each project specified in the subparagraphs of Article 8 (1) of the Act.
(3) Where deemed necessary in consideration of the conditions for promoting the mining industry or implementing the relevant project, the president of the Corporation may reduce or exempt all or part of the project expenses calculated in accordance with the standards under paragraph (2).
(4) Prior approval from the Minister of Trade and Industry shall be obtained when determining the calculation standards under paragraph (2) or the standards for reduction or exemption under paragraph (3). <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 12 (Issuance of Corporate Bonds)
Where the Corporation intends to issue corporate bonds pursuant to Article 11 (1) of the Act, it shall obtain a resolution of the board of directors on the following matters:
1. The purpose of issuing the corporate bonds;
2. The method of issuing the corporate bonds;
3. The matters specified in Article 15 (2) 2 through 6.

Article 13 (Form of Corporate Bonds)
Corporate bonds issued by the Corporation pursuant to Article 11 (1) of the Act shall be in bearer form: Provided, That they may be in registered form at the request of a subscriber or holder.

Article 14 (Methods of Issuing Corporate Bonds)
Corporate bonds under Article 11 (1) of the Act shall be issued by offering, underwriting of the total amount, or sale.

Article 15 (Issuance of Corporate Bonds by Offering)
(1) A person who intends to subscribe to an offering of corporate bonds by the Corporation shall submit to the Corporation two copies of a corporate bond subscription form stating the number of corporate bonds to be acquired, the acquisition price (the offered price where the bonds are issued with a minimum price fixed), and the subscriber's address, and bearing the subscriber's name and seal or signature.
(2) The president of the Corporation shall prepare the corporate bond subscription form under paragraph (1), including the following matters:
1. The name of the Corporation;
2. The total amount of corporate bonds to be issued;
3. The par value of each type of corporate bond;
4. The interest rate on the corporate bonds;
5. The method and period of redemption of the corporate bonds and the method of paying interest;
6. The issue price or minimum issue price of the corporate bonds;
7. The total amount of unredeemed corporate bonds (limited to cases where any previously issued corporate bonds remain unredeemed);
8. The trade name and address of the company entrusted with the offering of corporate bonds (limited to cases where a company has been entrusted with the offering of corporate bonds).

Article 16 (Total Amount of Corporate Bonds to Be Issued)
When issuing corporate bonds, the Corporation may indicate in the corporate bond subscription form that the corporate bonds will be issued even if the total amount actually subscribed for is less than the total issue amount stated in the corporate bond subscription form. In such cases, the total amount subscribed for shall be the total amount of corporate bonds to be issued.

Article 17 (Payment of Acquisition Price of Corporate Bonds, etc.)
(1) Upon completion of an offering of corporate bonds, the Corporation shall, without delay, require subscribers to pay the full price of the corporate bonds they have subscribed for.
(2) Where the Corporation has entrusted the offering of corporate bonds to a company, the company entrusted with the offering may perform the act under paragraph (1) in its own name on behalf of the Corporation. In such cases, the company entrusted with the offering may prepare the corporate bond subscription form.
(3) Where corporate bonds are issued by offering, bond certificates shall not be issued until the full amount payable corresponding to the total issue amount has been paid.

Article 18 (Issuance of Corporate Bonds by Underwriting of Total Amount)
Where the Corporation issues corporate bonds by underwriting of the total amount, it shall enter into a contract on the method of underwriting the corporate bonds and other related matters with the person intending to underwrite those corporate bonds.

Article 19 (Issuance of Corporate Bonds by Sale)
(1) Where the Corporation issues corporate bonds by sale, it shall give public notice in advance of the sale period and the matters specified in Article 15 (2) 1 through 6.
(2) Where the total amount of corporate bonds sold during the sale period under paragraph (1) is less than the total amount of corporate bonds to be issued, the total amount sold shall be the total issue amount.

Article 20 (Matters to Be Stated in Bond Certificates)
A bond certificate shall state the following matters and bear the name and seal or signature of the president of the Corporation:
1. The number of the bond certificate;
2. The date of issuance of the bond certificate;
3. The matters specified in Article 15 (2) 1 through 5 (excluding the matter specified in subparagraph 2 of that paragraph where corporate bonds are issued by sale).

Article 21 (Corporate Bond Register)
(1) The Corporation shall keep at its principal office a corporate bond register stating the following matters:
1. The quantity and numbers of bond certificates by type;
2. The date of issuance of the bond certificates;
3. The matters specified in Article 15 (2) 2 through 5 and 8.
(2) Where bond certificates are in registered form, the Corporation shall enter the following additional matters in the corporate bond register, in addition to the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1):
1. The name and address of the owner of the bond certificates;
2. The date of acquisition of the bond certificates.
(3) An owner or holder of bond certificates may request to inspect the corporate bond register at any time during the Corporation's business hours.

Article 22 (Missing Interest Coupons)
(1) Where an interest coupon is missing upon redemption of bearer corporate bonds with interest coupons, the amount corresponding to the missing interest coupon shall be deducted from the redemption amount.
(2) A holder of an interest coupon under paragraph (1) may claim payment of the amount deducted from the redemption amount under that paragraph in exchange for the interest coupon.

Article 23 (Notices to Holders of Bond Certificates, etc.)
(1) A notice or demand to a subscriber or a person entitled to rights before the issuance of bond certificates shall be sent to the address stated in the corporate bond subscription form: Provided, That where the Corporation has been separately notified of an address, the notice or demand shall be sent to that address.
(2) A notice or demand to a holder of bearer bond certificates shall be given by public notice: Provided, That where the holder's address is known, the notice or demand may be sent to that address.
(3) A notice or demand to an owner of registered bond certificates shall be sent to the address stated in the corporate bond register: Provided, That where the Corporation has been separately notified of an address, the notice or demand shall be sent to that address.

Article 24 (Transfer of Earned Surplus Reserve, etc. to Capital)
Where the Corporation intends to transfer an earned surplus reserve or a business expansion reserve to capital pursuant to Article 12 (3) of the Act, it shall obtain approval from the Minister of Finance and Economy after a resolution of the board of directors. <Amended on December 30, 2025>

Article 25 (Operation of Overseas Assets Account)
"Purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13 (4) 3 of the Act means the following purposes:
1. Payment of taxes, including national taxes, imposed on projects of the overseas assets account;
2. Expenses incurred in the operation and management of the Overseas Assets Management Committee under Article 10 (2) of the Addenda to the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (Act No. 17919) (hereinafter referred to as the "Overseas Assets Management Committee");
3. Funds deemed necessary by the Overseas Assets Management Committee for projects of the overseas assets account.

Article 26 (Requests for Statistical Data)
Where necessary to efficiently carry out the mineral products stockpiling business under Article 8 (1) 12 of the Act, the Corporation may, pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act, request the Commissioner of the Korea Customs Service to provide statistical data on imports and exports of mineral products, specifying the purpose of use, the content and scope of the data, the method of provision, and other relevant matters.

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 31961, August 31, 2021>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on September 10, 2021.

Article 2 (Repeal of Other Statutes and Regulations)
The Enforcement Decree of the Korea Resources Corporation Act is hereby repealed.

Article 3 (Expert Members of the Overseas Assets Management Committee and Composition of Its Secretariat)
(1) The term "experts in the sale of assets related to investments in overseas mineral resources prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (3) 2 of the Addenda to the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (Act No. 17919) means persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on October 1, 2025>

  1. A person who is or was a public official of Grade III or higher in charge of affairs concerning energy and underground resources;

  2. A person with at least 15 years of work experience at an institution, corporation, organization, or similar entity related to overseas resources development, finance, law, accounting, or financial management;

  3. A person with at least 10 years of work experience in affairs related to his or her qualification after obtaining a qualification as an attorney-at-law (including a foreign lawyer under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Foreign Legal Consultant Act) or a certified public accountant;

  4. A person with at least 10 years of work experience at a university or an accredited research institution in affairs related to his or her degree after obtaining a doctoral degree in resources development, finance, law, accounting, or financial management;

  5. Any other person recognized by the Minister of Trade and Industry as having expertise equivalent to that specified in subparagraphs 1 through 4.

(2) A person meeting the requirements concerning expertise under Article 10 (6) of the Addenda to the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (Act No. 17919) shall be a person falling under any subparagraph of paragraph (1).

(3) The secretariat under Article 10 (7) of the Addenda to the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (Act No. 17919) (hereinafter referred to as the "secretariat") shall have one director, who shall be designated by the Minister of Trade and Industry from among public officials in general service belonging to the Ministry of Trade and Industry. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

(4) The director of the secretariat shall take overall charge of the affairs of the secretariat and direct and supervise its staff under the orders of the chairperson of the Overseas Assets Management Committee.

(5) Where necessary for the performance of the affairs of the secretariat, the chairperson of the Overseas Assets Management Committee may request the secondment or concurrent appointment of public officials or employees belonging to relevant administrative agencies, research institutions, organizations, or similar entities, in consultation with the heads thereof.

(6) Matters necessary for the operation of the secretariat, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (5), shall be prescribed by the chairperson of the Overseas Assets Management Committee in the operating regulations of the Overseas Assets Management Committee, following a resolution of the Overseas Assets Management Committee.

